<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>White River Canyon from Timberline Lodge</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:130-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.331129" lon="-121.711243"><ele>1813.1</ele><name>Timberline Lodge</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:timberline-lodge (OSM way 149173768); confidence: high; pdf_page: 132; book_elev_ft: 5950; quote: Climb behind the lodge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.333800" lon="-121.710000"><ele>1847.8</ele><name>North of the lodge, west lip of the first gully</name><desc>source: about 300 yards north of the lodge (DEM 1,850 m), approach as in the companion tour 'Timberline Lodge to White River'; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 132; quote: From the northeast corner of the upper parking lot at Timberline Lodge, cross the road and ski northward climbing gently for about 300 yards to a very steep gully. Cross this potentially dangerous gully and head southeast, along contours to another similar gully that also must be crossed. Continue to the near edge of White River Canyon, which is perhaps 700 yards from your starting point.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.334000" lon="-121.707300"><ele>1819.1</ele><name>First gully (Salmon River headwaters) crossing</name><desc>source: DEM low 1,819 m on the ravine at 45.334; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 132; quote: From the northeast corner of the upper parking lot at Timberline Lodge, cross the road and ski northward climbing gently for about 300 yards to a very steep gully. Cross this potentially dangerous gully and head southeast, along contours to another similar gully that also must be crossed. Continue to the near edge of White River Canyon, which is perhaps 700 yards from your starting point. / 'cross a very steep ravine to the east. This is the headwaters of the Salmon River'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.333600" lon="-121.704500"><ele>1818.1</ele><name>Second gully crossing</name><desc>source: DEM low 1,821 m on the second gully at 45.334; reached southeast along the contours; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 132; quote: From the northeast corner of the upper parking lot at Timberline Lodge, cross the road and ski northward climbing gently for about 300 yards to a very steep gully. Cross this potentially dangerous gully and head southeast, along contours to another similar gully that also must be crossed. Continue to the near edge of White River Canyon, which is perhaps 700 yards from your starting point.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.333000" lon="-121.703000"><ele>1806.1</ele><name>Stand-off point near the White River Canyon west edge</name><desc>source: DEM 1,806 m, about 150 m west of where the canyon wall drops (1,723 m at 45.332, -121.701); 0.65 km (about 700 yards) from the lodge; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 132; quote: From the northeast corner of the upper parking lot at Timberline Lodge, cross the road and ski northward climbing gently for about 300 yards to a very steep gully. Cross this potentially dangerous gully and head southeast, along contours to another similar gully that also must be crossed. Continue to the near edge of White River Canyon, which is perhaps 700 yards from your starting point. / 'Do not go near the edge!'</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>White River Canyon from Timberline Lodge</name><desc>1. Timberline Lodge -&gt; North of the lodge, west lip of the first gully: straight (medium), 0.19 mi | 2. North of the lodge, west lip of the first gully -&gt; First gully (Salmon River headwaters) crossing: straight (medium), 0.13 mi | 3. First gully (Salmon River headwaters) crossing -&gt; Second gully crossing: straight (medium), 0.14 mi | 4. Second gully crossing -&gt; Stand-off point near the White River Canyon west edge: straight (medium), 0.08 mi</desc>
